Modifications (October-November 2026):
- Ported the osu! stable memory reader from TypeScript and C++ to Rust.
- Removed the HTTP/WebSocket server, overlays, PP calculation and osu!lazer
  support.
- Exposed the result as a Rust library crate with its own public API, where
  each piece of game data is read on demand by its own method.
- Memory signatures are resolved lazily: only the ones needed for the
  beatmap are required when attaching, and missing ones are searched again
  in executable memory when first needed.
- Screen-specific readers check the game state before reading.
- The beatmap is discarded when it was read while the game was moving it in
  memory.
- Added translation of Windows paths through Wine drive mappings on Linux.
- Memory signatures are searched for by their longest run of fixed bytes
  (with memchr), then checked in full where it appears.

